{"name":"Le Grand Bleu","hex":"#244e94","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Large, senior (high-ranking), intense, extreme, or exceptional","Great in size, and fine or imposing in appearance or impression; illustrious, dignified, magnificent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thousand of some unit of currency, such as dollars or pounds.","A thousand RPM."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grand"}],"entries":[{"title":"Le Grand Bleu (yacht)","blocks":[{"text":"Le Grand Bleu is a superyacht. She was the 36th longest private yacht in the world in 2019, at 113 metres (371 ft) in length. She was built at the Bremer Vulkan yard in Bremen, Germany, and was launched in 2000. She was designed by Architect Stefano Pastrovich and constructed by Kusch Yachts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Le_Grand_Bleu2009-2-2.JPG/330px-Le_Grand_Bleu2009-2-2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Le_Grand_Bleu_(yacht)"},{"title":"The Big Blue","blocks":[{"text":"The Big Blue is a 1988 drama film co-written and directed by Luc Besson. Inspired by the Cinéma du look movement, the film is a heavily fictionalized and dramatized story of the friendship and sporting rivalry between two leading contemporary champion free divers in the 20th century: Jacques Mayol and Enzo Maiorca, and Mayol's fictionalized relationship with his girlfriend Johana Baker."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/93/The_Big_Blue_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Big_Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Le_Grand_Bleu2009-2-2.JPG/500px-Le_Grand_Bleu2009-2-2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik